  "notes": "The research calls this catalog a good source of 4-bar functional minor loops, and that is the parameter that separates it from the static-tonic half of this axis: real i–iv–V and i–VI–VII motion carried by progression families with a `1_per_bar` harmonic rhythm, not a vamp. The other two authored distinctives are the pronounced and-of-2 kick (`secondaryAnchor: \"2&\"`, which no other entry in this batch uses) and the marimba/steel-pan/nylon-guitar palette, taken as `marimba_pluck` because the dataset names no steel pan. Hats are weighted toward the triplet vocabulary the research describes, and the tambourine/rim percussion layer is authored because the research names those two lanes specifically. ⚠ `medium` because the research rates this high-medium. ⚠ The 808's slow portamento is INFERRED as `slideProb` 0.6 with scale-step slide intervals (m3/P4/P5): the research says it follows the guitar/marimba root by portamento but gives no rate. ⚠ The minimal-drums *Super Gremlin* lane is not authored as a separate mode — the research describes it as one beat type inside the catalog, not a weighted half of it. ⚠ `anticipationProb` raised to 0.15. With `mirror_kick` against a fully locked 808 both parts take every kick, so every bass onset lands exactly on an 808 onset — `coherence.rs` calls that one line played twice rather than two parts locking. The lock is the style and is untouched; the anticipation is what makes them two parts.",
